#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2228 expect=violation domain=MI
#note "MIRESCAT is not in the dataset at all while MISTRESC carries an abnormal finding -- the guarded variable's column is ABSENT ENTIRELY. Under EC-43 an absent column is all-missing, so empty(<var>) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports its defect on the rows its other conjuncts select. The variable was removed from Requirements.Variables.All on 2026-08-27 (owner ruling) because it is Permissible in this domain and NO rule anywhere reports its absence -- neither a specific presence rule nor the generic Required/Expected rules, which do not cover Permissible variables. Before that removal this scenario would have taken a silent dataset SKIP."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset MI class=FINDINGS label="Microscopic Findings"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col MISEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MITESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col MISTRESC type=Char label="Standardized Result"
---
S1 | MI | 001 | 1 | MIEXAM | INFILTRATE
